Conservative min/max cloud hierarchy
===================================

Authority and scope
  Source: docs/PBR.CloudHierarchy.Proposal.md (approved design).
  Parent: docs/PBR.BaselineShading.todo, cloud hierarchy acceleration evaluation.
  Existing cloud implementation: docs/PBR.Clouds.md and docs/PBR.VolumetricClouds.todo.
  The proposal governs scope. Every task remains unchecked until its stated evidence exists.
  Accelerate view and existing solar/lunar self-lighting rays without changing native weather,
  cubic column bounds, procedural fluff, PMJ sampling, lighting or six-attachment OIT composition.
  Keep shared scene-depth HZB foreground clipping and full-resolution texture-only resolve intact.
  Do not add a 3D density volume, scene-HZB format change, CPU map readback, native-method hooks,
  or cloud shadows cast onto the scene; those shadows remain deferred to virtual shadow maps.

Execution conventions
  Keep files domain-focused, resource ownership explicit and composition roots thin. Follow
  repository comments and visibility regions, dedicated shader program/binding contracts and
  existing GPU resource, submission, shader registration and cleanup APIs.
  Run build/test tools through subagents. Use focused lightweight correctness checks routinely;
  full-size reference captures and GPU timing belong to explicit qualification work below.
  Never launch the game for visual acceptance; the user performs live acceptance.
  Distinguish source inspection, CPU oracle, GPU correctness, package and live timing evidence.
  Reconcile linked documents and perform a second review before marking an increment complete.

Implementation choices and acceptance inputs
  RG32F, native leaves and conservative min/max reduction are fixed by the approved proposal.
  Select the GPU reduction submission mechanism and traversal implementation through existing
  rendering APIs; these are implementation choices, not authorization for a new GPU abstraction.
  Use the current native publication contract, not assumptions based on texture names or uploads.
  Target hardware, resolutions, representative scenes and performance budgets are not specified.
  Record those targets before performance acceptance; do not invent numbers or block math work.

Phase 1: Establish hierarchy contracts and independent bounds oracle
  Outcome: storage geometry, source identity and conservative reduction have executable checks.
  ✔ Reverify native inputs and current VGE consumers against the installed producer.
    - Trace CloudMapInput, CloudMapPublication, CloudPlacement and CloudColumn validity semantics.
    - Confirm 50-by-50-world-unit cells, one interval per texel, red extinction and BA tile units.
    - Record odd/non-power-of-two dimensions and animated GPU bounds; neither CPU short controls,
      thickness limits nor world placement establish equal neighboring heights or voxel alignment.
  ✔ Define logical hierarchy geometry and certificate semantics without duplicating native leaves.
    - Logical leaves occupy the next-power-of-two grid; out-of-map leaves are empty, never clamped.
    - Owned mip zero is logical level one, reducing 2-by-2 native columns. Higher mips reduce
      2-by-2 summaries; node footprint derives from logical level, not the owned mip index alone.
    - Convert valid native bounds to world units. Empty intervals use positive/negative infinity;
      reject invalid native texels exactly as density evaluation does and exclude zero extinction.
    - Retain every valid positive extinction, however small; never infer emptiness from sampled noise.
    - Define current-source matching for owner, world, allocation, executable, generation and placement.
  ✔ Add an independent CPU bounds oracle and focused contract checks.
    - Cover empty/sparse/dense inputs, nonfinite/negative controls, inverted intervals, separated
      heights, tiny positive extinction, odd widths, padding and mip-to-logical-level mapping.
    - Check every node encloses every occupied descendant using direct descendant enumeration.
    - Verify maximum 200-wide input implies logical 256 leaves and owned 128-through-1 storage:
      eight mips, 21,845 RG32F texels, approximately 0.17 MiB excluding allocation overhead.
  ✔ Completion: source receipts and passing focused checks establish geometry, validity, units
    and certificate contracts without changing rendering behavior.
    - Completed 2026-10-16 after second review and independent audit-stage-completion against
      the proposal and inherited documents. Native receipts and 35/35 focused passing checks
      are recorded below. Later implementation and live acceptance remain unchecked.

Phase 2: Generate and publish owned coarse summaries
  Depends on Phase 1. Outcome: current certified summaries are available before tracing.
  ✔ Implement the hierarchy resource owner and dedicated reduction shader/program contracts.
    - Allocate only coarse RG32F mips; borrow the native map read-only as logical leaves.
    - First reduction reads 2-by-2 native texels with explicit source bounds checks. Later reductions
      combine summary intervals; empty children never contaminate valid minima/maxima.
    - Preserve infinities for empty nodes and retain conservative bounds without filtering averages.
  ✔ Integrate GPU construction after successful native map generation and before VGE tracing,
    through the existing publication/draw boundary; do not tick or reschedule native weather.
    - Rebuild for every newly published generation, including in-place animation with unchanged
      CPU weather uploads. Reuse allocations across ordinary frames when layout remains compatible.
    - Order writes and sampling through existing GPU submission/visibility contracts, including
      dependencies between reduction levels. Publish only after all required writes are visible.
    - Withdraw stale/failed certificates; match the exact borrowed source immediately before use.
    - Retire owned storage on source/lifetime invalidation, world teardown, reload or disposal;
      native resources remain native-owned. Use existing DDA when summaries are unavailable.
  ✔ Compare GPU reductions with the independent oracle, including empty-root and padded-edge cases.
    - Exercise source replacement, reused texture names, failed generation/build, layout changes,
      executable invalidation and unchanged-allocation animated generations.
    - Test-only readback may verify results; production must not read map or hierarchy texels to CPU.
  ✔ Completion: focused build/shader/GPU checks pass; publication and fallback lifecycle checks
    show current summaries, no duplicate leaf allocation and no stale-resource sampling.
    - Completed 2026-10-16 after second review and independent audit-stage-completion against
      the proposal and inherited documents. The retirement finding was resolved and rechecked;
      fresh build/shader evidence and 82 distinct passing checks are recorded below. Later phases
      and live/performance acceptance remain unchecked.

Phase 3: Accelerate reduced-resolution view traversal
  Depends on Phase 2. Outcome: view rays skip conservatively without changing occupied integration.
  ✔ Add hierarchical traversal to the reduced trace shader and explicit trace bindings.
    - Reject rays missing the root; compare each remaining horizontal segment with the node height
      interval, skip only proven misses, otherwise descend and read native children at logical leaves.
    - Preserve original occupied-column intersections, interval boundaries, integration sample counts,
      sample order, PMJ indices and cell/view/light decorrelation. Do not index jitter by visited nodes.
    - Handle parallel axes, boundary ties, negative directions, padded regions and inside-cloud origins
      conservatively with guaranteed forward progress. Work limits must not silently discard density.
    - Select the original column DDA for unavailable/mismatched hierarchy data before accelerated use.
  ✔ Validate traversal independently of its own reduction and skipping helpers.
    - Compare ordered occupied intervals against direct column enumeration and existing DDA for
      adversarial and deterministic randomized rays, including near-tangent and exact-boundary cases.
    - Compare accelerated and original GPU view results under identical PMJ frames/settings, with
      detail enabled/disabled and current opaque/liquid clipping. Retain deterministic reference
      quadrature as an independent reference; do not turn full-resolution resolve into a ray marcher.
  ✔ Completion: interval and transport comparisons pass without altered sampling or weakened
    expectations, and missing summaries render through the existing DDA.
    - Completed 2026-10-17 after second review and independent audit-stage-completion against the
      proposal and inherited sources. Final build/shader evidence, 100 distinct passing checks and
      matching candidate hashes are recorded below. Secondary-light acceleration and later live
      correctness/performance gates remain unchecked.

Phase 4: Accelerate secondary self-lighting traversal
  Depends on Phase 3. Outcome: solar/lunar secondary rays use the same conservative summaries.
  ☑ Reuse hierarchy traversal for existing bounded secondary marches in accelerated tracing.
    - Preserve light-ray limits, occupied intervals, density evaluation, integration sample counts,
      solar/lunar decorrelation and PMJ dimensions; support off-camera rays and finite map exits.
    - Preserve the unaccelerated comparison path and existing fallback; add no cast-shadow consumer.
  ☑ Compare optical depths, illumination and all OIT payload channels with the original path using
    identical PMJ frames/settings, sun/moon directions, sparse/dense and separated-height maps.
    - Exercise horizontal/vertical lights, boundary starts, inside-cloud origins and long empty spans.
    - Independently check secondary occupied intervals; equivalent view output alone is insufficient.
  ☑ Completion: focused CPU/GPU checks establish view and secondary-light equivalence while
    foreground depth clipping, scene storage encoding and OIT composition retain existing contracts.

Phase 5: Qualify pipeline integration and reconcile documentation
  Depends on Phase 4. Outcome: the accelerated path is integrated with existing cloud lifetimes.
  ☐ Verify Off/Simple remain unaffected and Volumetric works in standalone PBR and PBR + LumOn.
    - Exercise mode changes, resize, reload, world replacement, resource/build failures and recovery;
      confirm no additional native hooks, premature native-resource disposal or duplicated generation.
    - Verify current-source matching through trace submission and reduced/history/resolve scheduling;
      preserve shared scene-HZB, primary/liquid clipping, temporal reconstruction and OIT targets.
  ☐ Run the canonical focused build/test/shader/package checks appropriate to changed components
    through subagents. Record commands, immutable candidate identity and results; distinguish
    pre-existing failures and unavailable runtime dependencies from verified behavior.
  ☐ Update PBR.Clouds.md to describe delivered ownership, reduction, traversal and fallback behavior;
    reconcile this checklist with the source proposal and parent without claiming live acceptance.
  ☐ Completion: integration receipts and second review cover the approved contracts; required
    correctness checks pass and remaining live qualification is explicitly tracked below.

Phase 6: Demonstrate end-to-end performance and live correctness
  Depends on Phase 5. Outcome: measured evidence establishes practical benefit and limitations.
  ☐ Record target GPU/hardware, resolution, settings, build identity, scene matrix and budgets.
  ☐ Measure original versus accelerated rendering on the same candidate and identical PMJ frames.
    - Include hierarchy construction plus view/light tracing in total cloud cost; separately record
      construction, trace and unchanged reconstruction costs without omitting setup overhead.
    - Include empty, sparse, dense overlapping and separated-height maps; ground, inside-cloud and
      above-cloud views; moving sun, weather and padded edges. Report regressions as well as wins.
    - Record owned memory and resource reuse. Hierarchy size alone does not establish acceleration.
  ☐ Obtain user-run live acceptance of shape, fluff, lighting, temporal stability, fog, foreground
    clipping and OIT composition in both PBR modes; do not infer appearance from headless checks.
  ☐ Reconcile any correctness or performance failures within approved scope and repeat affected
    checks. If benefit is not demonstrated, leave performance acceptance open and report findings.
  ☐ Completion: recorded total costs demonstrate benefit against agreed targets, live acceptance
    is recorded and limitations are explicit; no unresolved required gate is marked complete.

Final acceptance
  ☐ Every proposal requirement maps to delivered behavior and evidence, with no unsupported scope.
  ☐ Independent bounds/traversal checks and GPU transport comparisons pass; native leaves, padding,
    source certification, fallback and lifecycle behavior satisfy the approved design.
  ☐ Required build/shader/package checks, documentation, live acceptance and measured performance
    are complete. Reconcile parent checklist state only to the extent these receipts establish it.

Phase 1 contracts and source receipts
  Reverified installed inputs on 2026-10-16; assembly/shader hashes identify the inspected source
  independently of the older version label in the volumetric checklist.
  G:/Vintagestory/Mods/VSEssentials.dll SHA256:
    A28565C5C9181F8CC84B98A2B7457AB824B8ECB7763714448DA1F7C245AECD6E.
  G:/Vintagestory/assets/game/shaders/cloudmap.fsh SHA256:
    BE42585ADE68C57C1A3FF7E23687AC33B64E69D36B9AF225A1716C105F4CE0A7.
  CloudRendererMap constructor/CloudTick supply eight times desired view distance to InitCloudTiles;
  InitCloudTiles divides by CloudTileSize and clamps to 20..200 without power-of-two rounding.
  CloudRendererBase initializes size 50; cloudmap.fsh hardcodes 50. WriteTexture packs normalized
  short controls; shader main computes float heights and time-dependent undulation, writing red
  extinction and BA heights divided by 50. H is 0..405 for normalized controls, thickness is
  25+1.05*H, and undulation translates both bounds. These are not vertical quantization guarantees.
  WeatherPattern.RegenCloudTileCache samples per-cell noise, and WeatherDataReaderBase blends
  regional thickness; neither establishes uniform 2-by-2 groups. Native map extents remain finite.

  Task-to-document traceability
    Native verification -> proposal Representation; PBR.Clouds.md Borrowed map contract;
      PBR.VolumetricClouds.todo Phase 1 contracts/receipts and its source proposal's Column-data
      interpretation and Publication and native lifecycle -> installed methods/shader above,
      CloudNativeMapAdapter/CloudMapPublication and unchanged CloudColumn/CloudOccupied semantics.
    Geometry/certificates -> proposal Representation and Ownership and publication ->
      CloudHierarchyLayout, the test-side CloudHeightInterval and CloudHierarchySource. Intervals are relative to
      the cloud layer in world units, not absolute altitude; current CloudPlacement supplies the
      transform. Source matching includes reference owner, world, allocation, upload, shader,
      generation, frame, storage and placement. A fresh native borrow and completed GPU-build
      certificate are separate requirements; source equality alone certifies neither availability
      nor completion. Resource construction/publication remains Phase 2.
    Independent oracle/checks -> proposal Acceptance; parent cloud bounds/empty-space scope ->
      CloudHierarchyBoundsOracle directly enumerates native descendants without production reduction
      or layout helpers. Bounds tests compare every coarse summary with those exact extrema;
      layout tests cover all admitted widths, and source tests exercise identity changes and
      generation withdrawal without a new weather upload. No rendering caller uses these contracts
      yet, so scene-HZB, PMJ, atmosphere, OIT, full-resolution reference and resolve stay unchanged.

