Phase 3 contracts and verification
  Task-to-document traceability
    Traversal/bindings -> proposal Traversal and Representation; PBR.Clouds.md Cloud height summaries;
      inherited volumetric proposal Column-data interpretation and Publication and native lifecycle ->
      cloud_volume_hierarchy.glsl, cloud_volume_trace.fsh and the view loop in cloud_volume_transport.glsl.
      Root/node rejection retains the original ray entry/end. Logical levels equal owned mip+1;
      finest summaries lead to actual native columns. Group skips reproduce original per-axis
      repeated-addition clocks and tied-axis events without fetching skipped native columns.
      Nodes already covering the current parameter descend without exit-clock replay. An exhausted
      defensive region budget returns to leaf work, never silently discarding remaining density.
    Admission/fallback -> proposal Ownership and publication; current native publication contract ->
      ICloudTraceBindings/CloudTraceProgram retain optional sampler 8 and an explicit availability/root
      block on Material slot 15, separate from temporal slot 14. CloudVolumeReconstruction revalidates
      the source and queries completed summaries before submission; missing/mismatched data clears
      the binding and selects DDA. CloudVolumeRenderer supplies the owned hierarchy. No additional
      native hooks, map copies, CPU readbacks or independent weather updates are introduced.
    Interval/sampling/transport preservation -> proposal Acceptance; parent cloud scope;
      PBR.Atmosphere.Publication.md Ownership -> CloudHierarchyTraversalTests exercises the production
      helper through a registered compute fixture, compares exact ordered GPU intervals against
      original GPU DDA, checks native probe reduction and compares independently enumerated column
      boxes. HierarchicalViewMatchesOriginalReducedTransport compares all seven traced channels
      at identical PMJ frames with detail on/off, opaque/visibility/liquid clips and source-mismatch
      fallback. Full-resolution midpoint reference, secondary lighting, density, scene HZB,
      atmosphere, OIT weighting and history/resolve remain unchanged.

  Independent geometry qualification
    On the 200-wide fixture, origin (50,0,50) and direction
      (.97014254,9.701425e-11,.24253564) expose existing native float-DDA corner slivers:
      cell (108,28), t=5566.1924..5566.199; cell (184,47), t=9483.143..9483.168.
    Direct double-precision geometry classifies those cells as tangencies. The accelerated and
      original GPU interval arrays agree exactly, including these original rounding artifacts.
      The renderer was not changed to force agreement with an exact-real geometric oracle.
    CloudTraversalOracle now qualifies every returned cell and both endpoints against its direct
      box projection using gamma_(width+4)*max(1,abs(t)), with unit roundoff 2^-24. This bounds
      slab subtraction/division, delta division and at most width positive clock additions for
      these fixtures. Unique ordered positive intervals are required; every independent interval
      longer than twice that bound must be present in order. Geometric tangencies/near misses can
      admit only individually bounded rounding-sized slivers. No accelerated-vs-original interval
      tolerance or transport tolerance was introduced; both GPU comparisons remain exact.
    The optional height sampler initially rejected DDA submissions when absent. Its required flag
      is now false and explicit availability disables all hierarchy reads. The final four actual
      transport cases verify absence/mismatch fallback as well as accelerated transport.

